50060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","color":"447777","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":17,"created_at":"2024-11-13T19:48:04Z","updated_at":"2025-06-15T20:19:32Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\r\n\r\nReproducible in: v4.3.stable.official [77dcf97d8]\r\n\r\n### System information\r\n\r\nGodot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.19045 - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 7700 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.12019.1028) - AMD Ryzen 7 7700 8-Core Processor (16 Threads)\r\n\r\n### Issue description\r\n\r\nI wanted to create an RTS game similar to BFME, but I ran into the problem that the engine is terribly optimized when using many units with a skeleton and animation based on it. I created the simplest model with the simplest animation and only with them I already get 100 fps with 1k units and below 10 fps with 10k units. In this case, the GPU and CPU are practically not involved. I can't use RenderingServer because I don't see that skeletal animations are implemented there in any way, the documentation seems completely unfinished at this point.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Run scene.\r\n\r\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\r\n\r\n[reproduction.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17738473/reproduction.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99194/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.git